  "\"cbw_start_watch：宿主 timer 当排期通道\" = \"cbw_start_watch: the host timer is the schedule channel\"\n" +
  "\"desc§剪贴板\" = \"Read/write the system clipboard text.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§剪贴板与桌面状态\" = \"Clipboard text, idle reading and autostart state (read-only).\"\n" +
  "\"desc§原生消息框\" = \"A native modal message box normalizing the result to semantic enums.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§子进程与平台专属能力\" = \"Every capability in this group is implemented, but only some platforms have a counterpart: the buttons are all here and each one reports why it cannot run on this machine instead of hiding or pretending. pr_run works on all three (timeout and output capture); window control goes through wmctrl, night light through redshift or xrandr, clipboard watching polls xclip / xsel - all Linux X11 only; power profiles use powerprofilesctl on Linux and PowerGet/SetActiveScheme on Windows.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§定时器与延时任务\" = \"Host timer period table plus one-shot set_timeout; both self-reschedule.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§应用与文件\" = \"Installed app stats, common binaries and recent VS Code workspaces.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§应用自更新\" = \"A ready-made check -> available -> download -> install dialog (update_dialog): the component owns the state machine and the view, while network/disk actions are injected closures. The demo backend feeds fake results on timers and walks every state without touching the network; the real backend uses the library-side sys_update_actions wired straight into @sys.update_* (it pulls this repo's Release update.json - a 404 until CI's first app-v tag run, and that failure notice is part of the chain; a real install swaps files and restarts, so don't press Restart & install on unpublished versions). Known trade-off: sys runs subprocesses synchronously, so the UI stalls during large downloads (an async executor comes with the platform thread batch).\"\n" +
  "\"desc§开机自启动\" = \"Toggles the real autostart state (Linux ~/.config/autostart, Windows Run key).\"\n" +
  "\"desc§打开外部\" = \"Open URLs/files with defaults or chosen apps, and reveal paths in the file manager.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§文件对话框\" = \"A native modal file dialog; open echoes the path, save writes a line.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§显示器\" = \"Current modes and all outputs (read-only native data per platform).\"\n" +
  "\"desc§浏览器数据\" = \"Chromium history/downloads/bookmarks and Firefox history, read locally.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§系统与桌面\" = \"Read-only distro, machine, memory, uptime, desktop env, env vars, wallpaper and printers.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§系统信息与音量\" = \"System info plus volume read/set/mute with explicit unsupported handling.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§系统托盘\" = \"Tray left-click counts, right-click pops a menu, dispatched via a 200ms poll.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§系统通知\" = \"System notification center: plain and progress notifications; unsupported backends say so.\"\n" +
  "\"desc§防多开与唤起已有实例\" = \"One native channel per platform behind a single facade: Windows uses a Local-session namespace mutex plus a hidden window that receives WM_COPYDATA; Linux first contests a D-Bus well-known name and falls back to an AF_UNIX socket when there is no session bus; macOS uses the AF_UNIX socket. The board claims the id at startup. Read backend shows which channel won and how many wakes this process received; Wake self sends one to this very process and the next tick recalls the first page with a toast. Two-process check: run the same command again in another terminal - the second process prints SHOWCASE-INST and exits, the running window is recalled.\"\n" +
